# Progress Log

This file is sized for fast agent load. Keep it small and current.

## Rules

- "Current Verified State" is **rewritten in place** every session, never appended. It reflects `main` — global state, not per-assignee.
- "Recent Sessions" keeps the **last 3 sessions max** per the project (not per assignee), each in the 6-bullet template below.
- Every "Recent Sessions" entry must **name the slice it was about** (e.g. `feature-001`, `issue-002`, `concept-assignment`) and the assignee. Parallel work from different assignees on the same day is fine because each entry is unambiguously slice-tagged.
- When the file crosses ~150 lines or 3 recent sessions, move the oldest session(s) verbatim into `docs/04-project/slices/99-progress-archive/YYYY-QN.md` and link from "Archive".
- Per-slice narrative belongs in the matching plan under `docs/04-project/slices/02-exec-plans/features/active|completed/` (feature) or `docs/04-project/slices/02-exec-plans/issues/active|closed/` (issue) or `docs/04-project/harness/concepts/` (concept). `PROGRESS.md` references the plan; it does not duplicate it.
- Every session uses this template - anything longer goes in the plan:
  - Slice: (e.g. feature-001 / issue-002 / concept-assignment)
  - Assignee:
  - Goal:
  - Done:
  - Verified: (commands + outcomes)
  - Risk:
  - Next:

